<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33486" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pallĭdus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		palleo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>pale</i>, <i>pallid</i> (cf.:
			lividus, luridus). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vides ut pallidus omnis Cenā desurgat
					dubiā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 2, 2, 76</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ora buxo Pallidiora,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					4, 134</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Prop. 5, 5, 72</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Asturii scrutator pallidus auri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					4, 298</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. 1, 618</span></i>: recto vultu et pallidus, i.
			e. <i>well</i> or <i>sick</i>, <i><span class="en">Juv. 10,
				189</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oriens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					18, 35, 78, § 342</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">stellae, quae sunt omnium pallidissimae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 2,
					25, 22, § 89</span></i>
			.—Esp. of the Lower World: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pallida turba,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tib.
					1, 10, 38</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ditis profundi Pallida regna,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					1, 456</span></i>
			: pallida Leti loca, Enn. ap. <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 7, § 6</span></i>
			Müll. (Trag. Rel. v. 109 Vahl.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">equus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Apoc. 6, 8</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>That makes pale</i>, <i>pallid</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pallida mors,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 1, 4, 13</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
					5, 7, 36</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aconita,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					4, 322</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>Musty</i>, <i>mouldy</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vetustate ficus fit pallidior,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 67</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>Livid</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hospes inauratā pallidior
					statuā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat.
					81, 4</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Pale with love</i>, <i>in love</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Prop.
				4, 7, 28</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pallidus in lentā Naïde
					Daphnis erat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. A.
					A. 1, 732</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Am. 3, 6, 25</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Pale with fright</i>, <i>affrighted</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. H. 12, 97</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1,
		14</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
